{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"A\n    \n      Wizard Inside Console (Recommended)\n      The wizard is a new view mode within the existing /platform/console app. When a tenant has zero auth events, the console renders the wizard instead of the normal tenant detail view. Once complete, the wizard flag is saved to the tenant config and the normal console tabs appear.\n      \n      \n        \n          Pros\n          \n            Single app shell — sidebar, auth, state all reused\n            No new routes or server handlers needed for the wizard itself\n            Wizard state persists in the tenant record (server-side), not localStorage\n            Polling for first auth event uses existing API infrastructure\n            Easy to swap: wizard view → console tabs, same mount point\n          \n        \n        \n          Cons\n          \n            Console store grows — wizard state added to existing store\n            Wizard steps need their own sub-views within the console app","choice":"a","id":null,"timestamp":1774963377453}
